# r2dbsvc-api EnvironmentFile example -- stage 1 parallel deployment (8443).
#
# Public example only. Every value below is synthetic (example.invalid / clearly
# fake secrets). Never place a real host, port, credential, or DSN in this file or
# in the copy installed at /etc/r2dbsvc/api.env; per CLAUDE.md's Public Repository
# Security Gate this repository copy is treated as public from creation time.
#
# This file lists every variable from the composition-root environment contract
# (docs/design/R2DB_CREDENTIAL_PERSISTENCE_AND_COMPOSITION_ROOT_V1.md, P2-D5)
# explicitly -- deliberately not relying on inheriting anything from the ambient
# shell/session environment (handover §2.5). Install the real copy at
# /etc/r2dbsvc/api.env, owned root:root, mode 0600 (see DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md §2
# step 2) -- systemd reads EnvironmentFile as root before dropping to the r2dbsvc
# service account, so the service account itself never needs read access to it.
#
# This deployment's own /etc/r2dbsvc/api.env must use DIFFERENT values than
# whatever the existing VPS r2db-api implementation reads for its own secrets and
# DB targets -- same variable *names* are fine (systemd EnvironmentFile scoping is
# per-unit), but the same secret value or the same DSN target used by both
# processes would defeat the isolation this parallel deployment exists to prove.
# See DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md §6.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: credential verifier pepper.
#
# HMAC-SHA256(pepper, secret) is what PostgresCredentialStore compares against
# the stored verifier (P2-D1). Changing this value invalidates every previously
# issued credential's verifier -- all applications would need credentials
# reissued via `python -m r2db_api.ops issue-credential`. Generate with, e.g.,
# `openssl rand -base64 32` and store the real value only in a secret manager,
# never in this file's installed copy in plaintext outside the 0600 boundary.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_CREDENTIAL_PEPPER=REPLACE_WITH_SECRET_MANAGER_VALUE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: platform DB DSN, used by PostgresCredentialStore for per-request
# credential/application-enabled lookups (P2-D4). Must authenticate as the
# read-only r2dbsvc_api role (SELECT-only on applications/credentials) -- never
# as r2dbsvc_control. See DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md §3 for posture A (password DSN,
# shown here) vs. posture B (UNIX socket + peer auth, no password) -- the choice
# is an operator decision, not fixed by this example.
#
# Posture A (password DSN):
R2DB_PLATFORM_DSN=postgresql://r2dbsvc_api:REPLACE_WITH_SECRET_MANAGER_VALUE@127.0.0.1:5432/r2dbsvc_platform
#
# Posture B (UNIX socket, peer authentication, no password in the DSN) -- comment
# out the line above and use this form instead if posture B is adopted for the
# whole deployment (see DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md §3 for the pg_hba.conf / pg_ident.conf
# mapping this requires):
# R2DB_PLATFORM_DSN=postgresql://r2dbsvc_api@/r2dbsvc_platform?host=/var/run/postgresql

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: the comma-separated list of application slugs this process instance
# serves. Each slug here must already be provisioned (r2dbsvc_registry.applications)
# and enabled, and must have both DSN variables below defined -- an unregistered,
# disabled, or DSN-less slug listed here makes the process fail to start (P2-D5:
# "うるさく落ちる", loud failure over a silently partial process).
#
# Two example slugs below only to show the per-slug DSN pattern; a real
# deployment may serve one slug or many.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_SERVE_APPS=alpha,beta

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required per served slug: runtime and developer role DSNs
# (R2DB_APP_<SLUG_UPPERCASE>_RUNTIME_DSN / _DEVELOPER_DSN). Each names that
# application's own database directly (database-per-application --
# r2db-api/docs/POSTGRES_PROVISIONING_RUNBOOK.md §0), never a shared database
# with a schema qualifier.
#
# Posture A (password DSNs) shown for both example slugs below. If posture B is
# adopted, replace with the socket form shown in the R2DB_PLATFORM_DSN comment
# above, using each application's own runtime/developer role name and database.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_APP_ALPHA_RUNTIME_DSN=postgresql://r2dbsvc_app_alpha_runtime:REPLACE_WITH_SECRET_MANAGER_VALUE@127.0.0.1:5432/r2dbsvc_app_alpha
R2DB_APP_ALPHA_DEVELOPER_DSN=postgresql://r2dbsvc_app_alpha_developer:REPLACE_WITH_SECRET_MANAGER_VALUE@127.0.0.1:5432/r2dbsvc_app_alpha
R2DB_APP_BETA_RUNTIME_DSN=postgresql://r2dbsvc_app_beta_runtime:REPLACE_WITH_SECRET_MANAGER_VALUE@127.0.0.1:5432/r2dbsvc_app_beta
R2DB_APP_BETA_DEVELOPER_DSN=postgresql://r2dbsvc_app_beta_developer:REPLACE_WITH_SECRET_MANAGER_VALUE@127.0.0.1:5432/r2dbsvc_app_beta

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: per-application connection pool tuning (SharedPoolManager). Written
# out here, uncommented, at this codebase's current defaults (r2db-api/docs/
# POSTGRES_PROVISIONING_RUNBOOK.md §4) -- this file's own stated purpose is
# listing every variable explicitly rather than relying on unstated code
# defaults, so these are not left commented out even though the value shown is
# exactly what omitting them would already produce. Change the values only if
# the connection-ceiling arithmetic in that runbook says a different one is
# needed for this deployment's application count and the target cluster's
# max_connections.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_POOL_SIZE=2
R2DB_POOL_MAX_OVERFLOW=2
R2DB_POOL_IDLE_SECONDS=300
R2DB_POOL_CACHE_MAX=32

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: the number of uvicorn worker processes r2dbsvc-api.service
# starts (`--workers ${R2DB_WORKERS}` in its ExecStart=). A positive
# integer; no default -- unset, empty, zero, negative, or non-numeric stops
# startup naming this variable. It must not exceed the declared
# `process_ceilings.data` (startup refuses otherwise), and `concurrency` is
# declared `enforced` only while the two are EQUAL -- declare
# `ops declare-process-ceilings --data <this value> --control 1`.
# DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md §8 has the one-host rule, the signals never to send,
# and the connection budget per worker. 1 is the example value only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_WORKERS=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: the host-shared concurrency slot directory every worker opens.
# Must be the directory r2dbsvc-api.service's `RuntimeDirectory=
# r2dbsvc-api/slots` creates (owned by the service account, mode 0700,
# removed when the unit stops). The application checks it -- existence,
# owner, mode 0700, a working `flock` -- and never creates it; any mismatch
# stops startup.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_SLOT_DIR=/run/r2dbsvc-api/slots

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: platform DB's own small dedicated pool (P2-D4; also backs the
# durable `application_audit` writer, Q4 D-1(b)), separate from the
# per-application SharedPoolManager keyspace. Left UNSET here (unlike the
# pool variables above) -- unset, each worker process derives it from its
# own thread limit (`R2DB_THREAD_LIMIT` + 2, `role_pool_size`; 6 at the
# default thread limit of 4), the same size its connection budget counts
# (POSTGRES_PROVISIONING_RUNBOOK.md §20). Set it explicitly only to
# override that derived value.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2DB_PLATFORM_POOL_SIZE=6

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2DB_THREAD_LIMIT: `run_in_threadpool`'s own worker-thread limiter for
# this process' event loop (`http.py`'s `create_app(..., thread_limit=)`).
# Unset or empty defaults to `DEFAULT_THREAD_LIMIT` (4). A positive
# integer raises or lowers it; zero, negative, or non-numeric is a
# startup failure naming this variable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2DB_THREAD_LIMIT=4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REMOVED (Q4 phase WP-1, design docs/design/Q4_DB_SIDE_SINGLE_TRUTH_V1.md
# D-1): R2DB_AUDIT_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS / R2DB_AUDIT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS are no
# longer read at all -- this process now fails to start if EITHER is still
# defined in this file, whatever its value (an empty string included). The
# application_audit writer connection's statement_timeout / idle_in_
# transaction_session_timeout are now a PostgreSQL role setting on
# r2dbsvc_api itself (`ALTER ROLE ... SET`, migration 0008_platform_
# declarations_and_writer_timeouts.sql), checked at startup against this
# role's own actual effective value. Change both with:
#
#   python -m r2db_api.ops set-platform-timeouts --statement-ms <N> --idle-ms <N>
#
# (against R2DB_CONTROL_DSN, the provision role -- see r2db-api/docs/
# POSTGRES_PROVISIONING_RUNBOOK.md), then restart BOTH this process and the
# control-plane process (r2db_api.control_main) -- the read is a startup-time
# snapshot, not live (design U-3). This single command places the SAME two
# values on both r2dbsvc_api and r2dbsvc_controlplane; there is no per-role
# override. If either variable is present here at all, remove the line
# entirely (a commented-out line with no value still counts as absent).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: Phase 4 durable audit sink -- the bounded in-memory buffer for
# ordinary (buffer-class) data-operation success events, per process (D-4),
# and how often the composition root's own background thread flushes it
# (`DataService.flush_audit_buffer()`). Written out here, uncommented, at
# this codebase's current defaults for the same reason as the pool variables
# above. `R2DB_AUDIT_FLUSH_INTERVAL_S` is a latency knob only, never a
# correctness one -- see r2db-api/docs/POSTGRES_PROVISIONING_RUNBOOK.md §15.1
# for the row-count-per-instance arithmetic this buffer capacity feeds into.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_AUDIT_BUFFER_CAPACITY=1000
R2DB_AUDIT_FLUSH_INTERVAL_S=2.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional, default `unavailable` (CCR-14 WP-5, R-9): the deployer's own
# declaration of whether a `/control/v1` control-plane process
# (`r2db_api.control_main`, DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md §7) is running alongside
# this application-plane process at all. Allowed values are exactly
# `enabled` / `unavailable` -- any other value (including a mistyped one) is
# a startup failure, never a silent fallback to `unavailable`.
#
# Set this to `enabled` ONLY after the control-plane process is genuinely
# running and reachable (DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md §7 step 3) -- this process
# cannot verify that fact on its own; the authoritative check is always the
# control plane's own `GET /control/v1/capabilities`, never this declaration.
# Left at the commented-out default below, this deployment declares
# `control_plane: unavailable` and runs the application plane alone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2DB_CONTROL_PLANE_STATUS=unavailable

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: overrides the derived default (`surfaces.data.base_url` with
# its trailing contract `versioning.base_path` replaced by the
# contract's own `endpoints.operation_catalog.path` -- reachable behind
# the same reverse-proxy prefix, if any, `surfaces.data.base_url` itself
# already carries). Set it (the SAME value on both this process and
# r2db_api.control_main) only for a CDN-fronted copy of the operation
# catalog.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2DB_OPERATION_CATALOG_URL=https://api.example.invalid/v1/operation-catalog

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REMOVED (Q4 phase WP-1, design D-2): R2DB_DATA_BASE_URL / R2DB_CONTROL_
# BASE_URL are no longer read -- this process now fails to start if EITHER
# is still defined here, whatever its value. `surfaces` (both `data` and,
# when this deployment sets R2DB_CONTROL_PLANE_STATUS=enabled above,
# `control`) is now the SINGLE `surfaces` row in r2dbsvc_registry.
# platform_declarations (migration 0008), shared by BOTH this process and
# the control-plane process (r2db_api.control_main) -- declare it with:
#
#   python -m r2db_api.ops declare-surfaces --data-base-url <URL> \
#     [--control-base-url <URL>]
#
# (against R2DB_CONTROL_DSN, the provision role), then restart BOTH
# processes (design U-3, startup snapshot). --control-base-url is OPTIONAL
# -- omitting it declares no control surface (there is a real silent
# default: no `control` row). --no-control is accepted as the EXPLICIT
# spelling of that same omission (design §3.8 F-6's own message shows it),
# never required -- passing BOTH --control-base-url and --no-control at
# once is a usage error (exit 2). Re-declaring without --control-base-url
# (or with --no-control) removes the control declaration for the OTHER
# process too (it will then fail to start unless R2DB_CONTROL_PLANE_STATUS
# is also set to `unavailable` there). See r2db-api/docs/
# POSTGRES_PROVISIONING_RUNBOOK.md §10 for why neither process can detect
# a mismatch with the sibling process' own platform DSN on its own.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional, TEST-ONLY -- do not set this in a real deployment. Overrides the
# platform registry schema name PostgresCredentialStore/main.py look up
# applications/credentials under (default r2dbsvc_registry, the literal schema
# name migration 0005_credential_store.sql creates). Its only reason to exist
# is so this repository's own test suite -- which runs the real migration
# files with the r2dbsvc_ prefix textually rewritten to a random throwaway
# prefix, to avoid colliding with anything else in a shared local test cluster
# -- can point a built app at its own rewritten schema
# (r2db_api/src/r2db_api/main.py's docstring documents this same reasoning).
# A real stage-1 deployment always uses the real 0005-created schema and must
# leave this unset.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2DB_PLATFORM_SCHEMA=r2dbsvc_registry
